{"title":"Career Roadmap · Research Engineer","role":"Research Engineer","summary":"A Research Engineer in Neuro-Engineering/BCI develops and evaluates technologies that connect neural signals, biological systems, and computational systems.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. — Engineering & Technology","Course":"Neuro-Engineering / Brain-Computer Interfaces (BCI)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Research Engineer in Neuro-Engineering/BCI develops and evaluates technologies that connect neural signals, biological systems, and computational systems."},{"type":"p","text":"The field combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Neuroscience"},{"text":"Biomedical engineering"},{"text":"Signal processing"},{"text":"Electronics"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Human-computer interaction"},{"text":"Embedded systems"},{"text":"Robotics"},{"text":"Brain-computer interfaces"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Designing neural-signal acquisition systems"},{"text":"Processing EEG and other neural signals"},{"text":"Developing BCI algorithms"},{"text":"Building signal-classification models"},{"text":"Designing experimental protocols"},{"text":"Developing neurotechnology prototypes"},{"text":"Evaluating neural interfaces"},{"text":"Building real-time brain-signal applications"},{"text":"Conducting experiments and analyzing results"},{"text":"Publishing or presenting research"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Career note","text":"“Research Engineer” is a broad title. For advanced BCI research, a master's degree is commonly valuable and a PhD may be expected for independent research/scientist positions."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech / B.E.","Neurotech / BCI Research Intern","Research Engineer / Research Assistant","Neurotechnology Research Engineer","Senior Research Engineer","Te